<attribute name="version" nodeId="2a66bc18"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="39f5b4c9">&lt;p&gt;
    Use the sprint review meeting to discuss and review the incrementally completed work with the Scrum team and key
    stakeholders. The Product Owner will lead the meeting explaining what Backlog Items have, and have not, been completed
    during the sprint. The Development Team should then discuss any problems they encountered during the sprint and how
    they resolved them. Finally, the Development Team will present the Backlog Items that were completed, according to the
    Definition of Done, and answer any questions participants have about the increment of work.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Build common understanding of the product and the current situation. With this information, work with the stakeholders
    to determine the best Backlog Items to work on in the next sprint(s) in order to maximize value of the work completed.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    To conduct a successful sprint review session:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Invite all relevant team members (Scrum Master, Product Owner, Development Team, stakeholders)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Enable active participation from all attendees
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review the status of Backlog Items to understand what is, or is not, completed
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Present the completed Backlog Items to the stakeholders, allowing time to answer possible questions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review remaining items in the Product Backlog against the current situation and goals 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                With this in mind, foster collaboration among all participants to determine the goals and next steps for
                subsequent sprint(s) which also serve as valuable input for the upcoming sprint planning session
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="866ac7cf"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="68976e05">&lt;p&gt;
    The sprint review is:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Not intended to be a status meeting; only discuss recent developments in order to level set before agreeing upon
        next steps
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Akin to a focus group on completed work; solicit feedback and suggestions from everyone on how to gain more value
        from current and future functionality
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Likely to result in changes to the Product Backlog based on either results of the sprint or&amp;nbsp;stakeholder
        feedback 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Any actionable feedback to be implemented should be documented as a new Backlog Item or as additional
                details to an existing item, if applicable
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Open to all relevant stakeholders, including those who may fall into one of the below categories: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Users - those who actually use, or will use, the product being developed or enhanced
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                External customers - those who are paying to use the product when it is being sold/developed for external
                use
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Internal customers - those within the company responsible for allocating funding to the development effort
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="8b0c2e59"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="4cce7359">To review completed work for sign-off and discuss work to be done next in order to optimize the value and adapt the Product
Backlog accordingly.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="7cfa7faa"></attribute>
